{
 "note": "The veil bag's cases (modules/lockscreen/lock/VeilBag.js) and themectl's port of it (bag_draw / bag_parse) answer each the same: tools/dev/themectl_bag_parity.py B1. `in` is the call (draw: state, names, rnd -- the random numbers in the order they are asked for; parse: text), `want` the answer (draw: name, state, used = how many random numbers it took). The answers were VeilBag.js's when the table was written (2026-11-08).",
 "cases": [
  {
   "id": "fresh-bag-three",
   "why": "an empty bag: a new round is a Fisher-Yates shuffle, the first off the front",
   "in": {
    "op": "draw",
    "state": {
     "round": [],
     "remaining": [],
     "last": ""
    },
    "names": [
     "/w/a.png",
     "/w/b.png",
     "/w/c.png"
    ],
    "rnd": [
     0.9,
     0.1,
     0.5
    ]
   },
   "want": {
    "name": "/w/b.png",
    "state": {
     "round": [
      "/w/a.png",
      "/w/b.png",
      "/w/c.png"
     ],
     "remaining": [
      "/w/c.png",
      "/w/a.png"
     ],
     "last": "/w/b.png"
    },
    "used": 3
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "mid-round",
   "why": "a round in progress: the next of what remains, no random number used",
